+# Mixed negative state-4 bit-6 countdown recovery (v0150)
+
+## Scope
+
+v0150 extends the v0149 native `fa_game_info` recovery for mixed state-4 pairs at a negative shared threshold when the combined `+0x1a4` flags are exactly bit 6.
+
+v0149 admitted this family only when the global countdown byte at `0x0050a0b6` was zero. ROM-backed probes now show that the same recovered C path is exact when the countdown is nonzero as well, so the countdown restriction is removed.
+
+## Evidence
+
+Starting from the same controlled mixed-state matrix used by v0149, the countdown byte was changed from zero to one and each case was executed from `0x0001645c` to the task return boundary at `0x00010dcc` with the ROM executor and the native recovered task.
+
+The matrix covers:
+
+- state 4 on either fighter;
+- the other fighter in states `0,1,2,3,5,6,7,8,9,10,15,255`;
+- bit 6 on the state-4 fighter, on the other fighter, or on both;
+- runtime mode bit 6 clear and set.
+
+Result: **144/144 countdown-nonzero cases match exactly** in CPU state, memory, calls/returns, and architectural state. Together with the 144 v0149 countdown-zero cases, this family now has 288 exact ROM-backed differentials.
+
+A representative countdown-nonzero reference path reaches `0x00010dcc` in 21 ROM instructions. The native recovered block reports 19 recovered instructions internally while producing an exact final snapshot, consistent with the block/task accounting boundary used by the native executor.
+
+## Native change
+
+The mixed negative state-4 bit-6 selector no longer reads the countdown byte merely to decide whether native execution is allowed. Once the measured state/flag/threshold predicate is satisfied, `hybrid_execute_game_info_18644` is used for both zero and nonzero countdown values.
+
+Unknown mixed state-4 flag combinations remain fail-closed behind the interpreted fallback.
+
+## Regression
+
+The ROM-backed CTest suite remains green: tests 1-45 passed in the first run and tests 46-52 passed 7/7 in the continuation.
